-- title:
--   A label unit at an end of the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $C = \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, $X = \mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ for the scheme obtained by glueing $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ along their common open part, and $\mathcal{O}_z$ for the stalk of $X$ at a point $z$.
--
--   **Base data.** A prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. A field $L$ of characteristic zero, an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfies $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. A subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which, by `hH₁`, is the intersection of the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the group [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$) with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. An intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which, by `hK`, is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. A discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a henselian local domain with algebraically closed residue field and with $L$ as its fraction field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$. An element $j \in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathtt{jq}$ of the modular invariant $j$ (`hj`). A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ (`hϖ`), and an element $\varpi_t \in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **The supersingular maximal ideal.** A maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The rigidity package.** For a point $z$ of $X$ at which the image $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}_z}$, for a point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $\mathtt{ιFin}(y') = z$ (the canonical morphism of the finite chart into $X$) satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` at $y'$, the package asserts the existence of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$; a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$; power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$ (the form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)); and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_z$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map of $\mathcal{O}_z$ into its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathcal{O}_z$ for the germ map at $z$ on the open image of the finite chart, the following six groups of conditions hold. (R1) $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$. (R2) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every automorphism $\tau$ of $K/L$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` — that is, such that on every quotient of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of weight $k$ and level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ the action of $\tau$ is given, after any embedding $\iota$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, by the weight-$k$ slash action of the matrix $\mathtt{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix}\gamma_{00} & \gamma_{01}/q\\ q\gamma_{10} & \gamma_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ of $\gamma^{-1}$ — the subalgebra $C$ is mapped into itself by $\tau$. (R3) If moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, then the endomorphism of $C$ induced by such a $\tau$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$. (R4) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every such $\tau$ preserving $C$ and inducing the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining the maps $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ before and after applying $\tau|_C$; $\theta$ fixing every class $C(w)$, $w \in W$; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$, modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$; and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$. (R5) For integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each failing to contain at least one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element of the form $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct. (R6) For every prime $P$ of $S$ failing to contain at least one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a \in C$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$. Finally (R7) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the $q$-expansion of $j$ with all exponents multiplied by $q$ — lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the corresponding element of $C$ minus $a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$, and $e\bigl(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\, - a_0))\bigr)$ equals the class of $h$, where $\cdot$ denotes the element of $C$ given by `jqNModC L q`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` asserts this package for every such $z$, $y'$. Next, a particular point $z$ of $X$ with its $\varpi_z$, the hypotheses `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `hy'`, the supersingularity `hss'` at $y'$ and `hy'y : y'.asIdeal = y`, together with particular data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ (with `hu₁`, `hv₁`, `hf₁` as above) for which `hW₁` asserts exactly the conditions (R1)–(R7) at $z$.
--
--   **The blow-up centre and its ends.** An ideal $J$ of $C$ which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of those ideals of $C$ of the form: the preimage under $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, the infimum being over $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ as in (R2) which preserve $C$. An $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ which, by `hB`, is the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), subject to: `hR1` (two clauses) $C \le B$ and $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2` (three clauses) $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) the elements of $L$ lying in $W$ are exactly the images of $A$, $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, an element $b \in C$ lies in $y$ if and only if it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_W$ (every $f \in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$).
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` has five clauses. First, for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,k$ (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by $(\mathtt{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$) whose vanishing locus is exactly $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, which is compatible with $A \to k$ and the structure map, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c \in \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathtt{hAction}\,q\,k\,(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c) \circ \rho$ on $B$, and $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$. Second, $B$ is stable under every $\tau$ attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ is reached: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ has $\tau(b) \in B$ and $\tau(b) \in Q$. Fourth, if $b \in B$ is carried into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by every $\tau$ attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, then the image of $\varpi$ divides $b$ in $B$. Fifth, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ on $C$ then $f \in W \iff \tau f \in W$ for all $f \in K$.
--
--   Finally, a subring $O$ of $K$ subject to: `hO`, which provides an element $a \in J$, nonzero in $K$, a maximal ideal $P$ of the $A$-subalgebra $B_a$ of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : xa \in J\}$, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, every element of $y$ which lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B$ is not contained in $O$; `hOW` $O \subseteq W$; `hOloc` and `hOnoe`, that $O$ is local and Noetherian; `hCO`, that $C \subseteq O$; and `hIgStab`, which requires that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose elements of $L$ are exactly the images of $A$, with the image of $\varpi$ in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, with $C \subseteq V$ and with some $c \in C$ such that $p(c)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[T]$, one has $f \in V \iff \tau f \in V$ for all $f \in K$, all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists $u \in C$, nonzero in $K$, with the following four properties.
--
--   (i) $u$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$: there are $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and $z \in C$ with $uz = \varpi^k$ (the image of $\varpi^k$ under $A \to C$).
--
--   (ii) $u$ is invariant: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every automorphism $\tau$ of $K/L$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, one has $\tau(u) = u$ in $K$.
--
--   (iii) For every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose elements of $L$ are exactly the images of $A$, such that the image of $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ whenever it lies in $V$, and such that $j \in V$ with $p(j)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[T]$: if $O \subseteq V$, then $u$ is a unit of $V$, i.e. $u \notin \mathfrak{m}_V$ whenever $u \in V$.
--
--   (iv) For every $V$ as in (iii): if instead some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$, then $u \in \mathfrak{m}_V$ whenever $u \in V$.
--
--   The element produced is a label (or marker) unit for the end $O$ of the blow-up of the supersingular chart along the weighted centre $J$: a vertical element of the $j$-finite chart algebra, invariant under the automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, which is a unit at precisely those Igusa-type valuation rings of $K$ — the valuation rings of the components of the special fibre, characterised by having $A$ as ring of constants, $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal and $j$ with transcendental reduction — that contain $O$. It serves the analysis of the special fibre of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a small prime $q$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_verticalUnit_chartAlgFin_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_verticalUnit_chartAlgFin_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd).
